      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what is happening:\n- we enter S3: \n  motion_sense_suspend() called,\n    motion_sense_switch_sensor_rate_data() triggered with a 0ms delay (CONFIG_MOTION_SENSE_SUSPEND_DELAY_US)\n- while waiting, we enter S5:\n    when motion_sense_switch_sensor_rate_data is finally called, the sensors are not touchable anymore, so the ODR is not changed.\n\n\n1. It should not matter if we set the collection rate (ODR) to 0 or not when the sensor power line are switch off in S5, the sensor will never interrupt us anymore.\nCan you confirm that\n- 1.1 wait_us is at -1 in S5\n- 1.2 be sure the BMI160 is also power off in S5, in addition to LIS2DWL. You can try to access their WHOAMI register via i2c. \n\n2. In any case, I uploaded a new patch that may address the issue (crrev.com/c/2541892). Let me know if that helps.\n\nI confirmed on another DUT(volteer) that when the sensors are off in S5, with this patch, motion_sense task is not woken up. [using taskinfo from the EC console].",
